  "label": "Islamophobia Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme relies on the harmful stereotype that Muslim women, particularly those wearing hijabs, are associated with violence or terrorism. This is a common and dangerous form of Islamophobia that equates religious attire with danger, reinforcing prejudice and fear. The text 'nuns don't randomly explode' is a crude metaphor that weaponizes this stereotype by implying that Muslim women are inherently explosive or dangerous, while suggesting nuns are not, despite both wearing head coverings.",
